2. **No production, no demo, no hosted site, no HTTP to any hosted host, no `az`, no Kudu, no docker, no ssh other than git's own `core.sshCommand`.** The only outbound traffic is what `npm ci` / `npm rebuild`, `git fetch`/`git push`, GitHub GETs and the Jira GETs themselves do, plus the loopback servers the jest cells boot on `127.0.0.1`. Never the retired VM address, never the NexusAI demo or marketplace hosts. **Never set, read-to-change or touch the repo variable `CI_DEPLOY_ENABLED`, a secret, an environment, or the repo's Actions settings (condition 3).** Reading `actions/variables` and `environments` by GET to prove the premise is allowed.
3. **No message to any human.** No mail, chat or PR comment. No person's name and no decision-card id in STATUS, code comments, commit messages or branch names (say "the product owner"; git author fields carry a name: do not quote them). Nothing to the client. Client name: Datasec/NexusAI only. **Jira is READ ONLY for you (GET only; zero writes).**
4. **Never delete** (`rm`, `git branch -d/-D`, `--prune`, `update-ref -d`, `worktree remove`, `worktree prune`, `gc`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `checkout -- <file>`). Quarantine to `session-tools/b658/_quarantine/`. Never rebase, amend, squash or force-push. Never write in the shared checkout `2_Project_Files` (read `git status --porcelain | wc -l` before and after, equal; `core.fileMode=false` there). Never open, read or write another seat's tree or kit: `worktrees/b650-*` and `session-tools/b650` (M9, live), `worktrees/b6[0-9][0-9]-*` other than your own `worktrees/b658-fix`, `session-tools/b6[0-9][0-9]*` other than your own `session-tools/b658/`, and any `worktrees/**` you did not create (a finished seat's STATUS file and the Briefs evidence folders are read-allowed).
5. **Shell:** never type `cd` (a hook refuses it); absolute single-quoted paths (they contain `!`); `git -C`; read git with `--no-optional-locks`; `bash -c '...'` or a heredoc for chains and loops (zsh does not split an unquoted `$VAR`; a hook refuses it); `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; write `${VAR}:path`, never `$VAR:path`; no unquoted word starting with `=` (use `echo ----`); write STATUS and source files with the editor tool; never hand-edit `package-lock.json`. Never kill a process by basename: by pid/port plus cwd. Stop every process you start and record the ports free again.
